From: 77450danik <ddziuba1@stu.vistula.edu.pl>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 23:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] server: A new window is in no band and not composited as a
 child.

The two bits that Arctic added to struct window were never set when a
window was made, and alloc_object does not clear its memory: once
another bit moved them, a window could be born in the band over program
windows and was made topmost. Every window ended up topmost, Progman too,
so SetShellWindowEx refused it, GetShellWindow stayed NULL and
"explorer C:\" started a second shell instead of opening a folder.
---
--- a/server/window.c
+++ b/server/window.c
@@ -739,6 +739,8 @@
     win->is_full_screen = 0;
     win->is_orphan      = 0;
     win->set_foreground = 0;
+    win->composited     = 0;
+    win->band           = 0;
     win->text           = NULL;
     win->text_len       = 0;
     win->paint_flags    = 0;
